      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":134,
          "quote":"The preferred realisation shape is functionally biased (P1, P6). That means semantic meaning should live in typed carriers and\nexplicit transforms; imperative coordination should be subordinate to\nadmitted truth; side effects should be isolated to explicit boundary\nmodules; and mutable shared state should be minimised and justified. The\nprofile does not require a functional programming language; it does\nrequire a functional design discipline.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPosition",
