      "statement":"AS-7/L-AS7: multiplying miss rates or promoting injected-defect scores to whole-Product correctness requires model, justified dependence and calibration scope; unsupported quantification stays unresolved while bounded observations survive (FOUNDATIONS §4 quantified assurance). AS-8/L-AS8: finite successes/schema-valid formula are no universal preservation proof; formal obligation, discharged argument, structure and bounded execution retain distinct scopes, with bounded work allowed under governing conditions (FOUNDATIONS §4 formal representation; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9 condition 1). AS-9/AR-04/L-AS9: changed governing requirements trigger owner-authorised reassessment of affected assertions/applicability; original evidence/counterexamples retain subjects (FOUNDATIONS §4 change impact; ACTIVATION §7). AS-10/L-AS10: impact includes material execution/validity dependencies, not just requirement-to-test provenance; missing influence cannot justify exclusion, uncovered obligations generate work and mandatory gates remain (FOUNDATIONS §4 change impact). AS-11/L-AS11: supported isolated repair permits unchanged applicable evidence plus affected reassessment, without automatic full rerun. AS-12/L-AS12: selection accounts for required assurance, residual uncertainty and total relevant cost; broader execution is available, and cheap selection/fixed full-suite habits prove neither adequacy nor efficiency (FOUNDATIONS §4 change impact/quantified assurance). Every case receives local logical review and actual-use evidence where its claim requires it; finite-model properties stay within declared model/population, mechanical validity grants no semantic fidelity or whole-Product conformance. Execution records independently bind current subjects/evidence; mapping neither proves pass nor exempts material owners/consumers from review.",
