          "quote":"For a product governed by the\ngraph-execution profile, this profile does not authorise replacing a graph\nfunction, edge traversal or graph module with deterministic implementation\nmodules; it governs the deterministic realisation shape inside or beneath\nthose carriers",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPurpose",
          "start_line":115
        }
      ],
      "key":"realisation_design_scope_and_bias",
      "statement":"The profile biases toward low coupling, modular composition, immutable typed carriers, total or nearly total semantic transforms and explicit effect boundaries, pursuing implementation discipline beyond passing code rather than language ideology. Every intermediate traversal should have a finite inspectable reasoning/implementation/evaluation/proof/refactor unit; modules are one tool, not the only possible bounded traversal. The profile governs ontology, architecture and module derivation after selected outcomes/capabilities, without replacing SPEC_METHOD constitutional authority or graph-native law. Required functionality does not determine entity/function/public-operation/carrier/module counts. For graph-profile Products, deterministic modules cannot replace graph functions, edge traversals or graph modules by this profile's authority; it governs deterministic shape within/beneath them. Scope includes the named boundary/schema/entity/interface forms and is not limited to one language/runtime.",
